  "job_B1.3.6_20251001_193223": {
    "text": "XIII KALENDAS FEBRUARII.\nPASSIO SANCTI SEBASTIANI MARTYRIS.\nSEBASTIANUS HATTE SUM HALIG GODES \u00f0EGN se w\u00e6s lange on lare on Mediolana byrig, and\nHe w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e snotor wer and so\u00f0f\u00e6st on spr\u00e6ce, rihtwis on dome and on r\u00e6de foregleaw, getreowe on\nD\u00e6ghwamlice he gefylde his drihtnes \u00feenunge geornlice, ac he bediglode swa \u00feeah his d\u00e6da \u00feam casere\nHe lufode swa \u00feeah \u00f0one halgan w\u00e6r, nyste \u00fe\u00e6t he gelyfde on \u00feone lifigendan God.\nHe gesette hine to ealdre ofer an werod, and het hine symble beon \u00e6tforan his gesih\u00f0e.\nAnd ealle \u00fea hyredmenn hine h\u00e6fdon for f\u00e6der and mid lufe wur\u00f0odon, for\u00f0on \u00fee God hine lufode.\nHe folgode \u00feam kasere uncu\u00f0 him swa \u00feeah, na swylce he ne dorste for his drihtne \u00f0rowian, ac he\n\u00dea geseah Sebastianus hu sume \u00fea Cristenan woldon awacian for \u00f0am orm\u00e6tum witum, and gehyrte\n\u00dea w\u00e6ron twegen gebro\u00f0ra \u00e6\u00feelborene for worulde, Marcus and Marcellianus, mycclum geswencte on\nHi sceoldon \u00fea underhnigan nacodum swurde, ac heora frynd ab\u00e6don fyrst \u00e6t \u00feam gerefan \u00f0rittigra\n\u00dea bet\u00e6hte Chromatius se heahgerefa \u00fea cnihtas sumum \u00feegne to gehealdenne se hatte Nicostratus.\nTranquillinus hatte \u00feyssera halgena f\u00e6der, and heora modor w\u00e6s Martia gecyged, h\u00e6\u00f0ena \u00fea gyt, and\n\u00de\u00e6r comon eac heora magas and mid manegum tihtingum \u00fe\u00e6ra cnihta mod fram Cristes geleafan\nHeora wif eac b\u00e6ron heora bearn him on handum, and axodon mid wope hwi hi swa w\u00e6lhreowlice\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a la ongunnon \u00fea godes cempan hnexian and heora mod awendon to hyre maga sarnysse.\n\u00d0a geseah sona Sebastianus \u00fe\u00e6t, hu \u00fea godes cempan ongunnon hnexian for \u00feam mycclan gewynne,\nNe awurpe ge ic bidde eowerne beorhtan sige for wifa sw\u00e6snyssum o\u00f0\u00f0e for cyldra tearum.\nAr\u00e6ra\u00f0 eower sigebecn fram eor\u00f0licum gewilnungum, and onginna\u00f0 eower gefeoht ongean \u00f0a\n\u00deas \u00fee her nu wepa\u00f0 woldon mid eow blissian, gif hi geare wiston \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t ge nu witon; hi wena\u00f0 to\n\u00deis lif is swa swicol \u00fe\u00e6t hit symble bep\u00e6c\u00f0 \u00fea \u00f0e hit swi\u00feost lufia\u00fe and geleafan him to habba\u00f0.\n\u00d0ises lifes gewilnung gel\u00e6t \u00fea unst\u00e6\u00f0\u00f0ian to manegum leahtrum and to mislicum frecednyssum.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to \u00feam magum \u00f0e \u00fea martyras mistihton, Gif nu \u00feas gebro\u00f0ra be eowrum benum gebuga\u00f0\n\u00de\u00e6r is wop and wanung and \u00fe\u00e6s ne wur\u00f0 nan ende.\nGe\u00feafia\u00f0 ic bidde \u00feisum gebro\u00ferum nu, \u00fe\u00e6t hi \u00feas witu forbugan and beo ge embe \u00fe\u00e6t ylce.\nL\u00e6ta\u00f0 hi nu faran to \u00f0am forestihtan kynehelme, and ne beo ge ofdr\u00e6dde; ne beo\u00f0 hi fram eow\n\u00c6fter \u00feissere lare and o\u00f0rum langsumum spr\u00e6cum, com leoht of heofonum to \u00f0am halgan w\u00e6re, and\n\u00dea wurdon hi ealle \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t wundor ablicgede.\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6gnes gebedda \u00f0e \u00fea gebro\u00fera heold, w\u00e6s for six gearum for swi\u00f0licre untrumnysse hire\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Sebastianus, gif ic so\u00f0 Godes \u00feeow eom, and gif \u00fe\u00e6t is so\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow s\u00e6de, geopenie \u00feonne\n\u00dea spr\u00e6c \u00fe\u00e6t dumbe wif, hire nama w\u00e6s Zoe, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t heo gesawe \u00feone scinendan \u00e6ncgel\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Zoe to Sebastiane eft, Eadige synd \u00fea \u00fee \u00feinum wordum gelyfa\u00f0, and \u00fea beo\u00f0 awyrigde \u00fee\nSwa swa d\u00e6gred todr\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00fea dimlican \u00feystra, and manna eagan onlyht \u00fee blinde w\u00e6ron on niht, swa\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Nicostratus wear\u00f0 swi\u00f0e afyrht, \u00fea \u00f0a he \u00fe\u00e6t wundor geseah on his wife gedon, and feol\n\u00dea ongunnon heora magas mycclum behreowsian \u00fe\u00e6t hi \u00e6fre \u00fea martyras misl\u00e6ran woldon, and\n\u00dea het Sebastianus \u00feone h\u00e6\u00f0enan \u00feegn \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fea h\u00e6ftlingas \u00fee he heold on \u00feam cwearterne gebrohte\nFerde \u00fea si\u00f0\u00f0an and gefette \u00e6nne m\u00e6ssepreost, Policarpus gehaten, halig w\u00e6r and snotor, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fea\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 gefullod se fores\u00e6da Nicostratus, mid his wife Zoe and \u00ferym and \u00f0rittigum mannum \u00fee him\n\u00c6fter \u00feisum wear\u00f0 gefullod \u00fe\u00e6ra martyra f\u00e6der Tranquillinus mid blysse, and his gebedda Martia,\n\u00d0\u00e6ra martyra f\u00e6der Marcellianes and Marces w\u00e6s endlyfan gear \u00e6r his fulluhte geuntrumed \u00feurh \u00fea\n\u00de\u00e6r w\u00e6ron eac untrume o\u00f0re tw\u00e6gen cnapan, o\u00f0er w\u00e6s w\u00e6terseoc, o\u00f0er eall on wundum; ac hi\nHi wurdon \u00fea ealle \u00feurh \u00fea wundra onbryrde, and on godes herungum hi sylfe gebysgodon, and\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Chromatius se mihtiga gerefa, \u00fee romana byrig under \u00feam casere geweold, het\nHe com \u00f0a gehaten to \u00feam heahgerefan, and eac ne bediglode \u00fe\u00e6t he on Drihten gelyfde.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se heahgerefa, \u00fee \u00fea git h\u00e6\u00f0en w\u00e6s, and eall swa yfele getucod swa Tranquillinus w\u00e6r \u00e6r,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Tranquillinus to Chromatie \u00feus, \u00fea godas \u00fee ge wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 w\u00e6ron arlease menn, yfele\nCwyst \u00feu la \u00fe\u00e6t n\u00e6re nan lyfigende God \u00e6r \u00fean \u00f0e Saturnus his suna abite, and heora fl\u00e6sc \u00e6te on\nEft his sunu Iouis, \u00fee ge wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 for God, se wolde acwellan his uncl\u00e6nan f\u00e6der \u00fee abat his gebro\u00f0ra\nLa hu ne dw\u00e6last \u00f0u, \u00fee on \u00feysum gedwylde gelyfst, and \u00feas arleasan menn arwur\u00f0ast for godas.\n\u00deu forl\u00e6tst \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan God \u00fee earda\u00f0 on heofonum, and cw\u00e6\u00f0st to \u00feam stane, \u00f0u eart min god.\n\u00dea gewende Tranquillinus aw\u00e6g \u00e6fter \u00feysum.\nAc se heahgerefa het hine gefeccan dearnunga on niht and him digellice bead anne gyldene wecg wi\u00f0\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Tranquillinus \u00fe\u00e6t mann Cristes gife ne moste syllan wi\u00f0 sceattum o\u00fe\u00fee swa gebicgan, ac\nChromatius \u00fea b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t he him gebrohte \u00f0one mann \u00fee hine gefullode and fram \u00fe\u00e6re co\u00f0e geh\u00e6lde.\nTranquillinus \u00f0a eode to \u00f0am arwur\u00f0an preoste, s\u00e6de hu hi spr\u00e6con, and hine sona gel\u00e6dde to \u00feam\nAnd he cw\u00e6\u00f0 him to, \u00feeah \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6s kaseres ehtnys \u00fea Cristenan gedrecce, \u00feeah for minre h\u00e6le ic sylle\n\u00dea hloh Policarpus and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam untruman, Crist m\u00e6g \u00feine nytennysse \u00feurh his miltsunge\nSe \u00f0e sceattas underfeh\u00f0 and syl\u00f0 Godes gife, se forde\u00f0 his sawle and se seoca ne bi\u00f0 geh\u00e6led.\nAc gelyf on \u00feone H\u00e6lend and l\u00e6t \u00fee fullian, and \u00feu bist swa gesund swa \u00fe\u00e6s Tranquillinus.\n\u00dea bead Policarpus him \u00fereora daga f\u00e6sten, and \u00feis sona s\u00e6de Sebastiane.\nHi \u00f0a begen b\u00e6don binnon \u00feam fyrste God, \u00fe\u00e6t he his geleafan geswutelode \u00feam seocan to h\u00e6le.\nComan him si\u00f0\u00f0an to and hine sw\u00e6slice gretton.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Sebastianus betwux o\u00f0rum spr\u00e6con, ne scealt \u00feu for \u00feinre h\u00e6l\u00f0e anre to \u00f0am H\u00e6lende\nDo \u00fein mod hluttor \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu leornian m\u00e6ge \u00feurh so\u00f0f\u00e6st gescead hwa \u00fein scyppend sy; ne miht \u00feu elles\nChromatius \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0, sume Cristene synd to \u00feam bilewite menn \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u ne miht afindan of anum\nHu mihton \u00feas becuman to Cristes geleafan?\nSebastianus cw\u00e6\u00f0, Crist geceas fram frym\u00f0e hyrdas and yr\u00f0lingas and anfealde fisceras, and hi si\u00f0\u00f0an\n\u00deu wur\u00f0ast manega godas and manega gydenan; butan \u00feu hi awurpe ealle fram \u00feinre heortan, and\nAc l\u00e6t us nu secan \u00feine sceandlican godas, and tobrecon \u00fea st\u00e6nenan and forbernan \u00fea treowenan,\nChromatius cw\u00e6\u00f0, ne cume ge to \u00feam teonan, ac ic bebeode minum \u00feeowum \u00fe\u00e6t hi hi ealle tobryton.\nSebastianus cw\u00e6\u00f0, hi ne cunnon \u00f0one geleafan, ne eac hi gebletsian, and bi\u00f0 se deofol geare hu he\n\u00dea \u00fee habba\u00f0 geleafan and leornodon to campienne ongean \u00feone swicolan feond unforhte \u00feurh God,\nChromatius \u00f0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam cenum Godes \u00feegnum, gewur\u00f0e Godes willa and eower eac \u00e6t \u00feysum.\nHi \u00fea sona begen begyrndon hi caflice, and to Gode geb\u00e6don, and tobr\u00e6con \u00f0a anlicnyssa ma \u00feone\nChromatius h\u00e6fde behydd on his digolnysse an wur\u00f0lic weorc on mechanisc geweorc, of gl\u00e6se and of\nSe cr\u00e6ft sceolde wissian gewisslice be steorrum hw\u00e6t gehwilcum menn gelumpe on his lifes\n\u00dea com Sebastianus and se sacerd Policarpus \u00e6ft to Chromatie, and gemetton hine untrumne, and\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea, ic h\u00e6bbe on minum hordcleofan an wundorlic weorc me to gewissunge, \u00e6fter steorrena\nOn \u00feam cr\u00e6fte aspende Tranquillinus min f\u00e6der of readum golde anum ma \u00feonne twa hund punda.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Sebastianus, se ges\u00e6liga martyr, Gif \u00feu \u00feisne cr\u00e6ft healst \u00feu bist \u00fee sylf unhal.\nChromatius cw\u00e6\u00f0, hw\u00e6t dera\u00f0 \u00feis \u00e6nigum?\nNe we hit ne wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 mid gewunelicum offrungum, ac hit gewissa\u00f0 us \u00feurh wisne lareowdom, to\nPolicarpus s\u00e6de \u00feis we forseo\u00f0, on \u00feam is so\u00f0festnysse gelicnys, ac hit is leas swa \u00feeah.\nSebastianus cw\u00e6\u00fe, \u00feis is swutol gedwyld and leas ydelnyss, swa swa we leornodon \u00e6t Criste.\nManega menn adrinca\u00f0 on anum d\u00e6ge tog\u00e6dere, \u00fee on mislicum tidum to middanearde comon.\nOft on anum gefeohte fealla\u00f0 for wel manige, \u00fee under anum tungle n\u00e6ron \u00e6r akennede.\nEft on anre tide twa m\u00e6dencild cuma\u00f0, and bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t an sydefull and \u00fe\u00e6t o\u00f0er sceandlic.\nNis \u00fe\u00e6t cl\u00e6ne herigendlic ne \u00fe\u00e6t gale tallic gif him steorran forgefon \u00fe\u00e6t hi swa lyfedon.\nFor\u00f0i synd laga ges\u00e6tte \u00fe\u00e6t menn rihtlice libban, and \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea rihtwisan beon geherode and \u00fea\n\u00dea wundrode Chromatius heora wisera worda and cw\u00e6\u00f0, se is so\u00f0 God, \u00fee swa gesceadwise\nHe ge\u00feafode \u00f0a \u00fe\u00e6t hi \u00fe\u00e6t weorc towurpon.\nAc his sunu Tiburtius sona mid gebeote cw\u00e6\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t he nolde nates hwon ge\u00feafian, \u00fe\u00e6t man swa\n\u00dea forbead se f\u00e6der \u00feone frecenfullan cwyde.\nAc \u00fea halgan tihton \u00fe\u00e6t man \u00fea ofnas ontende, and geb\u00e6don hi to Gode, and tobr\u00e6con \u00fe\u00e6t weorc.\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea f\u00e6rlice com f\u00e6ger Godes engel and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Chromati\u00e6, Crist me asende to \u00fee, on \u00feone \u00fee\n\u00c6fter \u00feysum worde he wear\u00f0 eall geh\u00e6led, and arn to \u00feam engle, wolde his fet gecyssan.\nSe engel him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, Ne cys \u00feu mine fet, ne \u00feu me ne hrepa, for\u00f0an \u00fee \u00feu ne eart gyt gefullod.\n\u00dea \u00fea se sunu \u00fe\u00e6t geseah, \u00fea gesohte he \u00fe\u00e6s preostes fet, and se f\u00e6der feoll to Sebastianus fotum,\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 gefullod f\u00e6der and sunu mid heora innhyrede, and heora \u00e6hta mannum, \u00e6g\u00f0res hades menn,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Chromatius, se Cristena \u00feegn, \u00fe\u00e6t he eallum gemiltsode \u00fee him \u00e6fre abulgon, and \u00feam\nHe freode ealle his menn and him feoh d\u00e6lde, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t he wi\u00f0 soce \u00feam gew\u00e6sum lustum\nHis sunu Tiburtius, se snotera cniht cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic awende minne willan fram eallum woruld\u00feingum to\nOn \u00feam dagum w\u00e6s sum wis papa on Rome, Gaius gehaten haliges lifes mann.\nWi\u00f0 \u00feone r\u00e6dde Chromatius and be his r\u00e6de underfeng ealle \u00fea Cristenan into his cafertune, and him\n\u00deam casere n\u00e6s \u00fea gyt cu\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Chromatius Cristen w\u00e6s, and he begeat \u00f0a leafe \u00fe\u00e6t he of \u00feam lande\n\u00dea bebead se papa \u00feam preoste Policarpe \u00fe\u00e6t he gewende of Rome mid \u00feam rumgyfolan \u00feegne, and\nFara nu se \u00fee wille for\u00f0 mid Chromatie, and wunige se \u00fee wille mid me on \u00feyssere byrig.\n\u00dea b\u00e6d Tiburtius \u00fe\u00e6t he beon moste mid \u00feam papan, cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t him wynsum w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6t he wurde\n\u00dea belaf Sebastianus on \u00fe\u00e6re byrig mid \u00feam papan, and se geonga Tiburtius and \u00fea tw\u00e6gen gebro\u00f0ra,\n\u00deas belifon on Rome on \u00fe\u00e6re re\u00f0an ehtnysse, and \u00fea o\u00fere ealle endemes ferdon aw\u00e6g, mid\n\u00dea gehadode se papa Tranquillinum to preoste, his tw\u00e6gen suna to diaconum, and \u00fea o\u00f0re to\nSebastianum he gesette him eallum to mundboran.\nHi wurdon \u00f0a gebysgode on heora gebedum ealle, d\u00e6ges and nihtes heora drihten herigende, biddende\nHi geh\u00e6ldon untrume mid halgum gebedum, and blinde onlihton \u00feurh heora geleafan, and of wodum\nTiburtius gemette \u00e6nne mann afeallene, \u00fe\u00e6t he his heafod tobr\u00e6c and eac his ban tocwysde.\n\u00dea sang he him ofer Pater Noster and Credan, and se mann sona gesundful aras, and beah to fulluhte\n\u00c6fter \u00feysum wear\u00f0 gel\u00e6ht seo eadige Zoe, and for Criste acweald and becom to his halgum.\n\u00dea o\u00f0re wurdon eac ealle gemartyrode.\nTranquillinus wear\u00f0 oftorfod mid stanum.\nNicostratus se \u00e6\u00f0ela wear\u00f0 \u00e6ft gel\u00e6ht, mid feower his geferum, and toforan \u00feam deman gebroht,\nHe axode \u00feone casere hu he embe hi sceolde, \u00f0a het se arleasa hi ealle fif pinian.\nFabianus \u00fea se feondlica dema \u00fea \u00f0e he ne mihte \u00fea menn gebigan fram Criste \u00feurh \u00fea re\u00f0an wita, \u00fea\n\u00c6fter \u00feysum wear\u00f0 gel\u00e6ht se geleaffulla Tiburtius.\n\u00dea het Fabianus \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00feam fulan Ioue recels geoffrode o\u00f0\u00f0e eode him sylf ofer byrnende gleda mid\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Tiburtius bealdlice eode ofer \u00f0a byrnendan gleda, unforb\u00e6rnedum fotum, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t him\nFabianus \u00fea, \u00fe\u00e6s feondes \u00feen, het beheafdian \u00feone halgan Tiburtium, and si\u00f0\u00f0an acwealde \u00feone\nHe geh\u00e6fte eft si\u00f0\u00f0an Tranquillines suna, Marcellianus and Marcus on anum micclum stocce, and mid\nHi sungon \u00fea sona \u00feisne sealm him betwynan, Ecce quam bonum et quam iocundum habitare fratres\nEala hu mycel god is and hwylc wynsumnys \u00f0\u00e6r \u00f0\u00e6r gebro\u00f0ru beo\u00f0 on annysse.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se gerefa \u00fee him swa re\u00f0e w\u00e6s, Eala ge unges\u00e6ligan and so\u00f0lice earmingas, alecga\u00f0 eowre\n\u00dea gebro\u00f0ra cw\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t hi on Cristes lufe \u00fea w\u00e6ron gef\u00e6stnode mid fulre blysse, and on swilcum\nHi stodon \u00fea stille on \u00feam stocce gef\u00e6stnode ofer d\u00e6g and ofer niht heora drihten herigende.\n\u00dea het Fabianus mid fullum graman \u00fe\u00e6t hi man begen ofstunge \u00fe\u00e6r \u00f0\u00e6r hi on gebedum stodon, and hi\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Fabianus mid facne gewregde \u00feone \u00e6\u00f0elan Sebastianum to \u00f0am arleasan casere Dioclitiane\n\u00dea het se kasere hine gef\u00e6ccan hra\u00f0e, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 him sona to mid swicolum ge\u00feance, Ic h\u00e6fde \u00fee mi